  "content": {
    "title": "Will NY’s Jesse Findling make top 12? 'American Idol' vote results revealed Monday",
    "text": "April 6, 2026, 4:38 a.m. ETOn Monday, America's votes will be revealed, determining the official top 12 contestants of American Idol Season 24, who will advance to the live performance rounds.Will New York's very own Jesse Findling make the cut?Here's what to know about the upcoming episode of American Idol, how to watch and how to vote.American Idol gets millions of votes at an 'unprecedented rate'Last week's episode of American Idol was a shock to both the viewers and those working on the show.Originally, the top 12 contestants, those who will move on to the live performance rounds of the competition, were supposed to be revealed. However, for the first time in the show's history, there were too many votes coming in to get an accurate count by the end of the episode.This season, fans have five different ways to vote: through Instagram, TikTok, Facebook, the official American Idol website and via text.\"Tens of millions of votes coming in at a rate we have never seen before. Truly unprecedented,\" American Idol Host Ryan Seacrest said during the March 30 episode.\"And to ensure complete accuracy with the numbers, I was literally just told we are not going to announce eliminations tonight,” the host continued. \"This is the first time it’s ever happened—believe me, I’ve been here every night.\"Now, the eliminated contestants will be revealed at the top of the April 6 episode.Who is NY's Jesse Findling?Representing New York for the 24th season of American Idol is 19-year-old Binghamton University student Jesse Findling.The Long Island native auditioned in Nashville in front of judges Luke Bryan, Lionel Richie and Carrie Underwood, earning a standing ovation and a golden ticket to Hollywood Week. During his audition, he shared how singing helps him overcome a stutter — a moment that resonated with both judges and viewers.His audition has also garnered nearly 4 million views on YouTube, adding to his growing national attention.Throughout the season, Findling has continued to blow away the judges and the viewers, receiving standing ovations after every performance.On the March 30 episode, Findling sang Rascal Flatts' Grammy Award-winning song, \"Bless The Broken Road,\" a song that judge Carrie Underwood sang on her own season of American Idol.Tune in on Monday, April 6, to see what Findling will perform next.American Idol's top 14. Who is up for elimination?The 14 contestants who will be up for elimination to determine American Idol's top 12 on the upcoming episode are:Philmon LeeBraden RumfeltJake ThistleJesse FindlingLucas LeonHannah HarperChris TungsethJulián KalelRaeDaniel StallworthKeyla RichardsonJordan McCulloughBrooks RosserKyndal InskeepAmerican Idol's new voting methods. How to vote for Jesse FindlingViewers can vote for their favorite contestants starting at 8 p.m. ET during the broadcast via five voting methods: the official voting site, idolvote.abc.com, American Idol's Facebook, Instagram, TikTik and by texting your favorite contestant's voting number to 21523. Findling’s voter number is 7.Voting opens at the top of the show and closes before it ends. Fans can vote up to ten times per voting method.When is the next episode of American Idol? How to watchThe next episode of American Idol Season 24 will air on Monday, April 6.American Idol premieres on Mondays on ABC at 8 p.m. ET, and streams on Hulu and Disney + the following day.Follow Jesse Findling's American Idol journey on his social media platformsInstagram: @jessefindlingmusicFacebook: facebook.com/JesseFindlingMusicTikTok: @jessefindlingmusicYouTube: youtube.com/@jessefindling— Madison Scott is a journalist with the Democrat and Chronicle who covers breaking and trending news for the Finger Lakes Region. She has an interest in how the system helps or doesn't help families with missing loved ones. She can be reached at MDScott@gannett.com.",
